id: SEC-025
title: Format string with user-controlled input (CWE-134)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .c .cpp .cc .h .hpp
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ .git/ build/
patterns:
  - regex: printf\(\s*[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*\)
    message: "printf() with variable as format string — enables arbitrary memory read/write (CVE-2012-0809)"
  - regex: fprintf\(\s*\w+\s*,\s*[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*\)
    message: "fprintf() with variable format string — format string vulnerability"
  - regex: syslog\(\s*\w+\s*,\s*[a-zA-Z_]\w*\s*\)
    message: "syslog() with variable format string — format string vulnerability"
fix: Always use a literal format string: printf("%s", user_data) instead of printf(user_data).